y.\""] [17592186394585 :question/problem "Solve for $\\mathbf{x}$ in $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ given that the matrix $A$ is orthogonal, and \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186394585 :question/worked-solution "The inverse of an orthogonal matrix is equal to its transpose.\n\nHence, since $A$ is orthogonal, we have ${A}^{-1}={A}^{T}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\mathbf{x} & =\\mathbf{b} \\\\ {A}^{-1}A\\mathbf{x} & ={A}^{-1}\\mathbf{b} \\\\ \\mathbf{x} & ={A}^{-1}\\mathbf{b} \\\\ \\mathbf{x} & ={A}^{T}\\mathbf{b} \\\\ \\mathbf{x} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\mathbf{x} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"]}
